00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:43.130
You go, all right, well, they
control the purse strings.

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:45.040
Let's introduce CRM tools.

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:47.660
Let's introduce our automation.

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:49.780
It's going to drive down
our contracting costs,

00:11:49.780 --> 00:11:53.422
and we'll have more revenue to
invest in, in additional areas.

00:11:53.422 --> 00:11:55.130
Or maybe because
they're federally funded

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:58.332
and their budget got cut this
year for a political reason.

00:11:58.332 --> 00:12:00.040
Or maybe you have
people who've seen this

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:03.340
before, CRM tools won't
fit within our mission.

00:12:03.340 --> 00:12:05.040
People won't adopt it.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:07.430
This is the same story
we've gone through again.

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:08.900
It doesn't work.

00:12:08.900 --> 00:12:10.450
Never does.

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:12.040
And then some
people, they've been

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:14.630
doing their job for 20 years,
and they don't want to change.

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:16.450
They think the way
they've created it

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:19.362
is the best way to get it done.

00:12:19.362 --> 00:12:21.070
And then some people
are-- let's be real.

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:22.000
There's the human element.

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:23.500
Some people, when
there's automation

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:27.140
in technology being introduced
that's new, they get worried.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:29.590
People have families to support.

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:31.600
They're worried about
job loss, right?

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:33.790
And so we need to take
into consideration

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:35.620
all of these different
stakeholders, all

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:38.650
of these different concerns,
all of these different risks--

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:41.600
the people, the
technology, the cost--

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:43.640
into how we actually
build the problems.

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:45.490
And so we think
rapid prototyping

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:49.330
is a really good way to do
this because we can fail fast.

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:51.010
We can build something
very quickly,

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:52.468
